WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.430
RANI URBAS: Hi, everyone.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.990
Welcome to the session
on Google Trust.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.960
We are part of the
Google Cloud Trust Team,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.030
and we work closely
with our customers

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.020
to ensure that you can
confidently use our products

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.870
and our technologies
from a trust perspective.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:27.130
Specifically, today will
focus on privacy, security,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.500
and compliance--

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.549
both industry best practices
and regulatory mandates--

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:38.040
data integrity, operational
transparency and user control.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.890
In this session, we'll
walk you through how

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.860
our Trust Team engages with
customers to achieve this.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.160
We have a very simple
agenda for you today.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.270
The introduction is really
focused on trust in the Cloud

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.540
and how that manifests
in everything that we do.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.350
We'll then delve
into the three C's.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.129
And you're probably wondering
what the three C's are.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:06.770
Without giving too much
away, we hope that we've

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.450
piqued your curiosity.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.240
And then we'll wrap by
sharing some resources

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.990
on where you can find more
information about Google Cloud

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:19.470
compliance, privacy
and security.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.320
By way of introduction,
my name is Rani Urbas.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.000
I lead the Enterprise
Trust team at Google Cloud.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.810
And as a team, we're responsible
for helping our Enterprise

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.380
customers in highly
regulated industries

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.460
with their compliance
and privacy and trust

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.880
related assessments
and implementations.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.850
We work closely with
our customers globally.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.540
And additionally, we assist
with customer-led audits,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.990
regulator audits--

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.650
which includes
data center audits.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:56.370
I am here with my
colleague Ruchi Khurana.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:00.390
And Ruchi leads the Google
[INAUDIBLE] Security Risk

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.320
program.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.030
And this program is focused on
ensuring the ongoing privacy

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.820
and security of
our customer data.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:14.280
She collaborates with many
of our highly regulated Cloud

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.860
Enterprise customers
on engagements

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:23.450
related to trust security,
audit and compliance.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.220
As I mentioned, I am part
of the Trust team at Google,

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.890
and our house is
built on four pillars.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:35.210
The first pillar is
around protection.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:40.370
Data security is the foremost
in everything that we do.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.380
It is part of our DNA.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.890
You've already heard,
probably, about our layers

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.240
of security controls.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.980
Our firewall, VPSC-- our
Virtual Private Cloud Service

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.210
Controls--

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.060
Cloud Armor, IAM--

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.770
Identity and Access Management--
with policy intelligence.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:03.890
And now, the Cloud
Security Command Center

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.190
Premium, with security
health analytics

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:11.510
to help with compliance and
misconfiguration detection.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:16.680
We've delivered additional
security functionality

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.840
with reCAPTCHA,
Enterprise, and Web

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.670
Risk, where we prevent ad
attacks, fake account creation,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.400
fraud, malware, phishing--

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.350
all that could
impact our customers

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.720
and our customers' end uses.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.020
Our second pillar, really,
is around transparency.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.440
The road to trust has to be
built through transparency.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:43.230
And that transparency has to be
based on accurate and on-demand

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.430
information.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.570
And we have built and delivered
features to our customers like

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.110
access transparency,
access approvals,

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:56.130
third-party key management
specifically for that reason--

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.730
products that enforce
customer control.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.490
Which leads us to
our third point--

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:03.540
control.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.520
We live by the principle that
our customers own their data,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.400
we don't.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.860
You can access it, take
it out at any time.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.730
We have built and
equipped our customers

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.779
with tools and technology
to manage access and protect

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:22.010
their data.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:25.460
And last, but not least,
is Enterprise compliance.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.860
We've built world-class
capabilities

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.760
to enable and facilitate
our customers'

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.440
compliance with a vast
range of regulatory bodies

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.550
around the world.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.240
We invest in achieving
and maintaining

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.560
our regulatory certifications
and attestations

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.400
for all of our products
across all of our data centers

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.150
globally.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.970
So for the purpose of
today's presentation,

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.570
we'll be looking at
trust through the lens

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:59.330
of our Enterprise
customer engagements.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:03.680
And for ease of discussion,
let's talk about it from,

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.550
one, a compliance perspective.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.110
two, a commitment perspective.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.950
And 3, the collaboration angle.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:17.270
Starting with compliance,
our customer-centric approach

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:20.630
to compliance has really
enabled us to view compliance

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.490
with a much wider perspective.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.940
So if you look at the
pyramid in front of you,

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:28.430
compliance of Google Cloud.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.480
We deliver foundational
certifications, as well as

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.910
industry-specific
certifications,

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.620
that addresses multiple
industry segments,

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.660
such as public sector, health
care, financial services--

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.190
to name a few.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.330
Over the foundation is
compliance in Google Cloud.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.530
We deliver a comprehensive
set of capabilities

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:55.310
to help customers ensure
that their Google Cloud

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:58.880
workloads are always compliant.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.990
Compliance toolkits, where we
deliver a very diverse range

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:08.570
of self-service compliance tools
to help our customers assess,

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:14.040
act and comply with their
regulatory requirements.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.660
So our customers and regulators
expect, as they should,

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:22.050
independent verification
of our security, privacy,

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.540
and compliance controls.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.380
And Google undergoes
independent, third-party audits

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:31.490
on a regular basis to
provide this assurance.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.100
This means that an
independent auditor

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:37.310
has examined the
controls present

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.760
in our data centers,
our infrastructure

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.730
and in operations.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:46.820
Our certifications
include widely recognized

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:51.570
and internationally-accepted
independent security standards,

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:56.750
including ISO 27001
for security controls,

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:04.640
27017 for Cloud security,
27018 for Cloud privacy--

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.280
as well as SOC 1,
SOC 2 and SOC 3.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.900
And these certifications help
us meet the demands of industry

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:17.000
standards also, such
as CSA Star, PCI DSS,

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.950
and many other regional
standards as well.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:23.240
And we continue to expand the
list of our certifications

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:27.890
globally to assist our customers
with their very dynamic

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.460
compliance landscape.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:34.210
Here's a list of some of
the regulatory authorities

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:37.090
that we've engaged,
both unilaterally,

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:40.490
and with our industry peers,
and with our customers.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:44.930
We're also working on more
compliance products and tool

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.830
links to help our customers
streamline and automate

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:50.860
their compliance process
with their regulators.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.170
So moving on, I'm
going to hand this over

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:57.190
to Ruchi, who's going to talk
about the second C in the trust

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.290
journey that we're
taking you on.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.252
Over to Ruchi.

00:08:00.252 --> 00:08:02.710
RUCHI KHURANA: Thanks, Rani,
for the wonderful introduction

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.590
and the summary on
the compliance piece.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.750
Now let's talk
about commitments.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.110
A major part of the
commitments is transparency.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:15.210
A Cloud providers should
detail how it operates.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:18.320
At Google, we are
committed towards providing

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.220
full transparency of
our security design

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:24.610
choices via multiple artifacts.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:29.110
A few recent examples include
our overall infrastructure

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.590
security, encryption
addressed and encryption

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.679
in transit across our platforms.

00:08:35.679 --> 00:08:39.789
When you have these types
of detailed documentations,

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:41.980
you can make the
decision yourself

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:46.690
to determine if what we are
doing for security and privacy

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.990
is adequate.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:54.880
Next, a Cloud provider should
provide binding commitments

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.750
on how it will operate and
handle your data internally.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.840
These areas of commitment
should include things

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:06.770
like processing restrictions,
business continuity, data

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.260
deletion, data incident
notification process,

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.080
subprocessor list, and
other security measures.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.360
At Google, we are
transparent and committed

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.040
towards all of these ideas.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.400
You can easily find
these commitments

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.505
on our data processing
security page.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.380
Now let's talk
about the third C--

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.530
that is collaboration, and
it's one of the most important

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:36.200
C's of the Trust.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:39.230
Talking about
collaboration, at Google,

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.660
we offer a suite
of services when

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.210
it comes to collaborations.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:46.430
To start with, we
have a huge team

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.490
of specialists who will
help you to understand

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:54.500
Google's GRC [? posture. ?] We
offer workshops and one-to-one

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.410
sessions with GRC gurus.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.240
An example would
be understanding

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.030
compliance lifecycle at Google.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:06.290
Secondly, we offer free access
to Google's third-party audit

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.250
reports--

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.090
which Rani mentioned earlier--

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:13.480
such as ISO, SOC,
FedRAMP, and others.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.220
Thirdly, our teams
work on a multitude

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.920
of security and
compliance collaterals

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:23.870
to help you understand and
address common security risks.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:26.840
Last, but not the
least, we are dedicated

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:28.790
toward supporting
your due diligence

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:33.230
on our third-party risk efforts
in the form of facilitating

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.480
your cybersecurity
risk assessments.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.450
Next, let me talk
through collaboration

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.240
through audit rights.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.220
At Google, we are
committed to meet

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:47.980
your regulatory and contractual
requirements of right to audit.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:51.290
We offer all regulated
customers right

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.410
to assess us on
security controls.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:59.750
Moreover, we also offer your
customers, or any users,

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.950
transitive right to
audit Google's services

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.760
and organization controls.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.360
Secondly, we understand
that your operations may

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:12.000
extend beyond a certain region.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.530
So we offer the right to
inspect a Google data center

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.370
for physical and environmental
security controls in whichever

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.050
region you are operating.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:27.170
Thirdly, we are committed to
support any audits that may

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.660
be requested by our regulators.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.690
What we have found
is that transparency

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.110
is the key when it comes
to working with regulators.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.890
And our teams will work with
you and support any request

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:43.040
with the utmost transparency.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.720
And finally, we also
offer pooled audits,

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:50.570
where multiple institutions
can pull together as one group

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:54.440
to audit Google services
an organization controls.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:58.370
This approach benefits both
Google and Google customers

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:01.910
in terms of time, resources,
level of effort and audit

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.060
depths.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.630
To give an example
of pooled audits,

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.700
Google is committed
toward supporting

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:12.080
CCAG pooled audits for European
financial institutions.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.360
These financial
institutions are required

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:17.720
to conduct a comprehensive
risk assessment of their Cloud

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:21.560
providers, to comply with
their regulatory obligations

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.790
from regulatory bodies
such as EBA or BaFin.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:29.030
To optimize on time
and cost of the effort,

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:31.640
these European
financial institutions

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.710
work together as a team.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:39.530
In 2019, we supported
Google's first CCAG audit.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.080
Audit planning and execution
took over six months

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.700
from both sides.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:47.810
Auditors collected over
800=plus documents.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:54.140
And 175+ Google-ers from from
24 different teams were involved

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.450
in supporting this audit.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:13:00.500
This shows how committed
we are to pooled audits.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.480
And 2020 pooled audits
is also coming soon.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.750
Now, when we talk about
Auditable Cloud Universe,

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.150
or any security
program firstly, there

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.850
are many areas of
responsibility.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.990
Starting from the base layer
of securing infrastructure

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:20.390
to going up in the stack
of securing the network,

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:23.210
securing data,
securing applications

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.940
or managing
identities and access.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.750
There are also ongoing processes
for security operations,

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.930
governance, risk and
compliance management.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.630
At Google, we
provide capabilities

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:39.260
to audit all of the domains that
are relevant for your business

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.800
operations.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.990
We have a global team who can
support you in any region--

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.410
be it Americas, Europe,
Japan, Asia-Pacific.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.520
We collaborate with local teams
on board policy and industry

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:54.950
to better understand
the regulations

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.700
that you are subjected to so
that we can provide the highest

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.250
level of services when it comes
to facilitating these audit

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.530
requests.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.930
Now here are some
additional resources for you

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:10.250
to learn more about Google's
security compliance and trust

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.500
posture.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.710
Thank you so much for
listening to us today.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:19.580
Hope you learned about how
Google Cloud is building trust

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:23.690
through compliance, commitment
and customer collaborations.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:24.990
Thank you.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:26.950
RANI URBAS: Thank you so much.

